# =============================================================================
# Build-context exclusions
# =============================================================================
#
# Keeping the context small is not only about speed. `.env` carries local
# credentials and MUST NOT be baked into an image layer
# (`TechArch/05-tech-stack.md` §8.4: "no credentials embedded in code or
# container images"); `.git` carries the entire history including anything ever
# committed. Both are excluded here rather than relied upon not to be COPYed.
# =============================================================================

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image, and a
# host node_modules built on a different platform would be actively wrong.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
build
coverage
**/coverage
.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. See the header.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and CI.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Planning and specification material — large, and irrelevant to a running
# container.
.planning
project_specs
docs

# Test artefacts.
test-results
playwright-report
**/*.e2e-spec.ts
**/*.spec.ts

# Infrastructure that is mounted at runtime rather than baked in. The Keycloak
# realm and the database init SQL are bind-mounted by docker-compose.yml, and
# the policy bundle is mounted into the OPA container — baking any of them into
# the API image would create a second, silently-stale copy.
infra
policy
Caddyfile
docker-compose.yml

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
.opencode
.tools
opencode.json
AGENTS.md
